================================================================================
  SECTION 4: BUGS FOUND AND FIXED (v7.0 → v7.1)
================================================================================

  [BUG-17] CRITICAL: cmd.exe goto :eof corruption
    PROBLEM: Using `call :log` inside a parenthesized `if` block caused cmd.exe
             to corrupt the batch file seek pointer, silently exiting the script.
    FIX:     Moved `call :log` outside of `if ()` blocks in the browser kill section.
    IMPACT:  Ultra Battery Saver runs reliably without random silent exits.

  [BUG-18] HIGH: Quick Re-apply [R] broke Power Saving Balanced mode
    PROBLEM: The Re-apply block hardcoded Ultra Saver values (40% CPU max, 
             EPP 100, 25% brightness). When users woke up the laptop from sleep 
             while in PSB mode and pressed 'R', it silently forced them back to 
             the laggy Ultra Saver CPU profile.
    FIX:     Made the Re-apply section mode-aware. It now branches based on
             `CURRENT_MODE` and re-applies either 100%/50% (for PSB) or 
             40%/25% (for Saver).
    IMPACT:  Users don't lose their smooth CPU experience after waking from sleep.

  [BUG-19] COSMETIC: Step Numbering Discrepancies
    PROBLEM: After Ferdium removal, Saver mode steps said `[1/16]` instead of 
             `[1/15]`. Balanced mode steps jumped from `[5/6]` to `[6/7]`.
    FIX:     Fixed all denominators (Saver is 15 steps, Balanced is 7).
    IMPACT:  Script looks professional and accurate.

